<!--
    Systematic vocabulary extraction pass over ISO 12100, second of the "high-yield norms first"
    batch (norm-product-classification skill, Workflow A). Every record cites its real source
    clause (queried live via find#NormClausesByDocument, not from memory).

    Real, honest finding: ISO 12100's corpus in this project is only 4 hand-transcribed clauses
    (provenanceClass=MANUAL_PARTIAL, no source PDF configured - see norm-sources.json) - a small
    fraction of the real standard. Of those 4:
    - 6.2.11.4 is already fully covered - it is the exact clause behind the 5 existing
      FEAT_NO_UNEXPECTED_START/FEAT_PARAMETER_INTEGRITY/FEAT_STOP_NOT_IMPEDED/FEAT_NO_EJECTION/
      FEAT_PROTECTIVE_DEVICE_INTEGRITY features in CyberMechanicalSafetyVocabularySeedData.xml -
      not redefined here.
    - 5.4 (hazard identification duty) and 6.2.11.1 (control systems shall be safe/reliable and
      resist operating stresses/external influences) are general design principles, not testable
      technical criteria - per Workflow A step 2's own discipline ("discard clauses that are
      process/policy language with no testable technical criterion"), no ProductFeature/
      ProductCategory is forced from them. A ProductCategory for "any machine with a control
      system" would also be near-universal and add no real classification value beyond what
      check#DeviceSafetyExposure already does structurally.
    - 6.2.11.7 (Software) is the one genuinely new, testable requirement in this small corpus -
      captured below.

    A full ISO 12100 pass would need the complete standard text, not available in this project
    yet (no source PDF) - this file reflects the real, limited corpus honestly rather than
    padding it with content sourced elsewhere.
-->
<entity-facade-xml xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/entity-facade-3.xsd" type="seed-initial">

    <mantle.product.feature.ProductFeature productFeatureId="FEAT_SOFTWARE_USABILITY" productFeatureTypeEnumId="PftSafetyFunction"
            description="ISO 12100 6.2.11.7 (Software): interactive software shall be designed to be easy to use and to avoid errors by the operator."/>

</entity-facade-xml>
